{"kind":"request","text":"C3 construction needs the ports that the note's scopeClient(handle, { signer, store, drafts }) sketch leaves implicit. A Signer holds only key and sign; a DeclaredHandle holds scope, at, definition and digest. Neither holds the member for predictionGrant, the service and membership for custody Identity, or the observation's authenticated context.\n\nProposal: ClientOptions extends ReplicaOptions with observe, takes signer, ClientCustodyStore, an explicit identity context { service, membership }, and actor: PredictionActor for the stand-in grant. It also takes a clock port { now, set, clear } so one timer can own send deadlines and schedule wakeups without sleeps in witnesses. Defaults use the wall clock. drafts is a small read port by key for the present values; C4 owns slots and mutation.\n\nFor C3's internal request operation, proposal: request(client, key, kind, values) lives in a source module that scope.ts does not export. Tests and C4 import it directly. scope.ts exports scopeClient, client view types, and the pure status function. It exposes no submit until C4. No new kernel export or wire shape. May I use these construction ports and internal seam?","body":{"conditions":"Rule on the C3 construction and request seam before the source fixes their public types.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}